    "Sample": {
      "Title": "Chronicles of the Northern March",
      "Subtitle": "An account of the deeds, peoples and perils of the frontier",
      "Author": "Gathered by brother Aldric",
      "Chapter1": "I · The Iron Pass",
      "Lead": "When the snow closes the pass, the March is left alone with its dead. The old folk say the first tower rose over a barrow, and that is why its foundations groan on moonless nights.",
      "Inline": "Captain <strong>Rodrik Vane</strong> swore to defend the garrison <em>to the last man</em>. In his diary he left <u>three warnings</u>, one of them <s>struck out in fury</s>, and the key <code>VIGIL</code> that opens the archive. More details in <a href=\"#\">the great chronicle</a>.",
      "Quote": "Whoever lights the beacon must be ready to see what comes to its light.",
      "QuoteBy": "March proverb",
      "After": "Since then nobody climbs the tower after sunset, and the old road is always walked in company.",
      "ListTitle": "Travel preparations",
      "ListIntro": "Before crossing the pass it is wise to gather supplies and keep to the marching order:",
      "Ul1": "Rations for <strong>six days</strong>",
      "Ul2": "Hemp rope and grappling hooks",
      "Ul3": "Oil for the lanterns",
      "Ol1": "Set out before dawn",
      "Ol2": "Ford the river by the <em>fallen bridge</em>",
      "Ol3": "Camp in the shelter of the tower",
      "Th1": "Place",
      "Th2": "Distance",
      "Th3": "Danger",
      "Row11": "Raven's Ford",
      "Row12": "2 leagues",
      "Row13": "Low",
      "Row21": "Grey Wood",
      "Row22": "5 leagues",
      "Row23": "Medium",
      "Row31": "Vane's Tower",
      "Row32": "9 leagues",
      "Row33": "High",
      "FoundryTitle": "Encounters on the road",
      "Foundry": "At the ford waits <a class=\"content-link\">Rodrik Vane</a>, who demands a toll from travellers. If the party refuses, roll <a class=\"inline-roll\">Persuasion 1d20+5</a> or prepare for a fight against <a class=\"content-link\">Raven Bandits</a>.",
      "SecretTitle": "For the GM only",
      "Secret": "Rodrik is no bandit: he guards the crypt key and lies to keep the curious away.",
      "MapTitle": "Map of the region",
      "Caption": "The Iron Pass and the old road",
      "Chapter2": "II · The Empty Tower",
      "Prose1": "Vane's tower stands where the road narrows between two walls of black rock. Its doors have stood open for three winters, and the snow has come in as far as the second landing with nobody to sweep it.",
      "Prose2": "Inside, the tables are laid, the pallets made and a draughts board lies half played. Nothing suggests a fight or a flight: only an orderly absence, as if the garrison had gone out to greet someone and never returned.",
      "Prose3": "In the high room the captain's notebook still lies open on the lectern. The last page says the beacon lit itself, and that from the walls they saw another light answer where there is no tower at all."
    }
